WEBVTT

00:05.100 --> 00:10.440
As of today, this pilot course will be doing investigative missions as Team Gargouille.

00:11.320 --> 00:17.450
From here on, you'll be going into the Lightless Realm to investigate it.

00:17.450 --> 00:20.450
As you previously learned,

00:20.450 --> 00:25.830
the Lightless Realm destroys the psyche of anyone who enters it.

00:25.830 --> 00:30.380
And to solve that problem, they developed...

00:31.550 --> 00:33.170
The Reaper?

00:33.170 --> 00:36.300
Sure, that's what they call it, but...

00:37.890 --> 00:40.770
Its offical name is "Argent."

00:40.770 --> 00:43.980
It's a prototype for a MA-Vess that's planned

00:43.980 --> 00:50.360
to have a special assistance system that makes activity within the Lightless Realm possible.

00:50.360 --> 00:53.530
It's an upgraded version of the Vess?

00:53.530 --> 00:54.030
Yeah.

00:54.030 --> 00:58.410
Yet they call it Reaper, and that's pretty sketchy, right?

00:58.410 --> 01:00.830
I mean, that Heito guy broke down too...

01:01.490 --> 01:04.160
He was broken from the start.

01:10.210 --> 01:15.760
I can't imagine that Isaku Heito, the same guy who murdered his entire family, is fit to being a pilot.

01:15.760 --> 01:16.470
Well, that's—

01:16.470 --> 01:19.510
It doesn't look like we're fit either.

01:21.260 --> 01:24.520
Still, something's off.

01:24.520 --> 01:29.770
The Reaper's seal being undone, and Akashi boarding it of all people, strike me as odd.

01:29.770 --> 01:32.030
Right! That's it!

01:32.030 --> 01:35.780
They even started testing Akashi as if this was planned.

01:35.780 --> 01:43.490
It didn't look like it was made to investigate anything, yet they still used it, right?

01:44.700 --> 01:47.960
The reason the Argent was created was to...

01:47.960 --> 01:51.170
...defeat Corpses or something?

01:51.170 --> 01:54.130
Is that really the reason?

01:55.630 --> 01:58.630
I remember hearing something of that sort.

01:58.630 --> 02:01.550
Hearing that this was a Corpse-combat course.

02:01.550 --> 02:03.560
No way!

02:03.560 --> 02:05.310
Corpses...

02:05.310 --> 02:10.270
Well, we were going to tell you eventually.

02:10.270 --> 02:16.990
The fact that machine was made
to combat Corpses is indeed true.

02:17.700 --> 02:19.610
You all are gonna do that too.

02:28.080 --> 02:33.670
The Dark Metal

02:28.080 --> 02:28.120
The Dark Metal

02:33.670 --> 02:38.090
Night turns to day, and day turns to night. Our wishes have wilted away

02:38.090 --> 02:42.260
Where did the person I want to meet go?

02:42.260 --> 02:46.720
Interlocking these fingers with my beloved

02:46.720 --> 02:50.480
Even though I can't feel them, I continue to live

02:50.520 --> 02:55.110
When the flower's petals

02:55.110 --> 02:59.240
Are plucked off by the wind's playful gale

02:59.240 --> 03:03.700
They are scattered in every direction

03:03.700 --> 03:09.040
Even if you long for it

03:10.040 --> 03:14.750
Don't disappear, just don't

03:14.750 --> 03:18.550
I can even give everything else away if I have to

03:18.550 --> 03:23.390
You were there, and I was there with you

03:23.390 --> 03:27.720
Let me take in these memories

03:27.720 --> 03:34.650
These brief moments are connected, turning it into eternity

03:52.250 --> 03:55.750
It's exactly because it's him that he was so fascinated by the Reaper.

03:52.500 --> 03:57.550
Episode 3
Seam of the Past

03:55.710 --> 03:57.630
It isn't a Reaper.

03:57.630 --> 03:58.880
Call it Argent.

03:58.880 --> 04:02.720
That aside, to think they were able to be in such synch.

04:02.720 --> 04:05.180
That was within expectations.

04:05.470 --> 04:11.770
We have many overlapping filters shutting
things out to keep its effects to a minimum.

04:12.100 --> 04:15.560
But it's true we're starting to see a breakthrough.

04:15.560 --> 04:21.820
We'll shut down the filters one by one and see how long he can hold on.

04:21.820 --> 04:25.030
This is his first day, so take it slowly.

04:25.030 --> 04:26.530
I guess.

04:37.630 --> 04:38.960
Stop it...

04:38.960 --> 04:40.130
Don't touch me...

04:43.930 --> 04:45.090
The strain is too much!

05:03.280 --> 05:05.570
Are you serious? That's all you've got?

05:18.000 --> 05:23.170
So, we are changing the team's formation to this.

05:23.170 --> 05:26.510
Saginuma-kun, you'll take the center.

05:26.510 --> 05:27.640
Hold on!

05:27.970 --> 05:30.510
What's the reason for changing the formation?

05:30.510 --> 05:33.470
Just because Akashi can pilot the Reaper?

05:33.810 --> 05:38.400
Well, pretty much.

05:39.020 --> 05:43.690
"Yes, those who can board the
Reaper are fascinated by death.

05:43.690 --> 05:50.030
To be loved by the Reaper,
one will not deny selling his soul."

05:50.030 --> 05:52.450
You just don't learn, huh?

05:57.250 --> 06:01.920
As we are a team, I don't think we should have just one person bear the burden of fighting the Corpses.

06:01.920 --> 06:04.710
That has already been decided.

06:04.710 --> 06:07.800
Is there a reason it has to be him?

06:07.800 --> 06:10.890
It seems to me that he's the only one <i>we know</i> can do it.

06:10.890 --> 06:11.890
Then do it!

06:12.510 --> 06:13.600
Fine by me.

06:13.600 --> 06:14.890
Go board it.

06:15.270 --> 06:18.600
Who said I was happy about the Reaper liking me?

06:26.690 --> 06:28.070
As expected.

06:28.570 --> 06:30.320
Let's switch now.

06:30.320 --> 06:32.660
Next up is Saginuma-kun.

06:33.780 --> 06:36.080
Hey, you look pretty pale.

06:36.080 --> 06:37.870
Is something wrong with you?

06:39.170 --> 06:40.290
Not really.

06:58.930 --> 06:59.940
Akashi!

07:00.520 --> 07:02.690
Hey, what's wrong? Are you all right?

07:10.990 --> 07:12.820
I heard you threw up.

07:12.820 --> 07:13.950
Are you okay?

07:14.740 --> 07:17.240
We did overwork you last night.

07:18.250 --> 07:21.830
It's not like you came by
because you were worried, right?

07:24.460 --> 07:27.000
You don't act cute at all.

07:27.000 --> 07:32.720
It's true they told me to check up on you, and maybe even bring you back with me.

07:32.720 --> 07:34.800
The Admonitions...

07:35.510 --> 07:38.930
They said they were memories left behind by the people who died...

07:40.730 --> 07:43.100
They appear because they're trapped by the past.

07:43.600 --> 07:45.230
I wonder if they're right...

07:46.900 --> 07:51.240
It's yet to be proven, but that's our educated guess.

07:52.320 --> 07:54.660
I don't like things like that.

07:55.620 --> 08:00.540
But whenever I'm on that thing, it feels like I'm getting trapped too.

08:00.540 --> 08:02.710
Like the past is dragging me down.

08:04.790 --> 08:05.630
I see.

08:06.500 --> 08:09.840
If I go, can you give me a reward?

08:10.340 --> 08:11.340
A reward?

08:12.220 --> 08:14.680
Sure, if it isn't impossible.

08:16.050 --> 08:18.390
It probably is.

08:20.390 --> 08:21.350
What is it?

08:22.060 --> 08:23.440
Just a joke.

08:23.440 --> 08:24.850
Let's go.

08:25.600 --> 08:29.440
Kasane-san, you told me to get on the Reaper.

08:31.990 --> 08:35.530
Why did you say that back then?

08:39.120 --> 08:41.080
It's okay if you don't want to tell me.

09:06.940 --> 09:09.690
If we defeat the Corpses...

09:11.440 --> 09:13.400
If we have the Reaper...

09:18.780 --> 09:26.290
I think we introduced you to her name
and photo during the briefing session...

09:26.290 --> 09:27.880
Please come in.

09:35.760 --> 09:37.090
That girl...

09:37.090 --> 09:41.260
We were a bit worried about her health, so the tests took longer than expected.

09:41.260 --> 09:44.730
Luckily she was cleared today to join Gargouille.

09:44.730 --> 09:46.850
She's Izuriha Sasame-kun.

09:48.100 --> 09:50.190
Nice to meet you all.

09:50.610 --> 09:53.030
Feels like I've seen her somewhere...

09:53.030 --> 09:55.400
Maybe she has a common face.

09:58.160 --> 10:00.120
Why are you staring so hard?

10:00.120 --> 10:02.410
Are you into girls like her?

10:02.410 --> 10:06.500
Well, in this group, normal is the new weird.

10:07.040 --> 10:09.210
What do you mean by that?

10:10.790 --> 10:13.550
You can sit on any empty desk.

10:13.550 --> 10:15.010
Thank you.

10:33.190 --> 10:34.610
Sasame!

10:36.360 --> 10:39.110
Sasame's a really weird name.

10:39.860 --> 10:43.740
Maki Minashi. My name's a bit weird too.

10:55.710 --> 10:57.720
Talk about poor taste...

10:58.630 --> 11:00.590
I'll head back first then.

11:00.590 --> 11:01.840
Sure.

11:02.550 --> 11:04.140
Keep stuff in moderation.

11:27.540 --> 11:29.410
Oh, you came.

11:29.410 --> 11:31.370
It was you?

11:31.370 --> 11:32.960
How so not you.

11:32.960 --> 11:36.550
The new girl calls you out and you show?

11:38.210 --> 11:41.970
You wanted to see what's the deal, despite knowing it was a prank.

11:42.840 --> 11:46.100
Are you that into her?

11:48.640 --> 11:49.680
Wait!

11:50.020 --> 11:53.270
I want to talk to you some more, Akashi.

11:53.270 --> 11:54.980
You're impossible.

11:54.980 --> 11:56.650
You just keep going at it.

11:58.280 --> 11:59.780
That's how I've lived my life...

12:01.950 --> 12:07.280
You know, there's something I want to show you...

12:08.040 --> 12:10.750
I want you to see it...

12:19.250 --> 12:20.630
There they are!

12:21.050 --> 12:22.840
Hey!

12:28.810 --> 12:29.850
How did you know?

12:29.850 --> 12:33.060
I have a sixth sense for this kind of stuff.

12:33.060 --> 12:33.980
Hurry!

12:37.060 --> 12:39.020
What were you doing?

12:39.020 --> 12:41.940
What? What were <i>you</i> doing?

12:42.820 --> 12:44.240
Ta-dah!

12:44.740 --> 12:46.990
I wanted to have fun with Sasame.

12:46.990 --> 12:49.450
Fireworks? Where'd you get that stuff?

12:54.420 --> 12:57.080
Yay!

12:58.250 --> 12:59.590
He's such a kid.

12:58.250 --> 12:59.590
Fireworks! They're fireworks!

13:00.550 --> 13:02.670
This is so beautiful!

13:04.130 --> 13:06.050
Did he force you?

13:06.390 --> 13:07.930
Not at all.

13:07.930 --> 13:10.850
I was happy he invited me.

13:10.850 --> 13:13.600
I don't have many memories of having fun.

13:16.650 --> 13:18.480
I see.

13:19.230 --> 13:22.360
Why did I do something like that?

13:35.910 --> 13:37.830
This is awesome!

13:37.830 --> 13:38.670
Having fun?

13:38.670 --> 13:40.210
I'm gonna do it again!

13:39.210 --> 13:40.210
Yeah.

13:41.170 --> 13:43.670
Can I ask you something strange?

13:45.220 --> 13:47.720
Have you heard of the Corpses?

13:48.430 --> 13:50.300
Or at least rumors of them?

13:50.300 --> 13:51.390
I have.

13:51.390 --> 13:56.310
Have you ever been on—have you ever seen one?

13:56.310 --> 13:57.520
No.

13:58.310 --> 13:59.310
No way you have.

14:00.150 --> 14:03.360
Sorry for asking something so strange.

14:04.230 --> 14:08.820
But I may have seen one in a dream.

14:17.290 --> 14:19.540
Would you like some fireworks?

14:20.250 --> 14:23.300
I guess it couldn't hurt.

14:34.930 --> 14:35.890
What are you doing?

14:36.180 --> 14:38.560
Three, two, one...

14:41.810 --> 14:43.110
That's not it!

14:43.110 --> 14:45.730
Who said you could fire there?

14:45.730 --> 14:47.030
Sorry...

14:47.030 --> 14:50.160
The formation isn't working at all!

14:50.160 --> 14:51.620
That's it! Swap!

14:51.990 --> 14:53.370
What's with this?

14:53.370 --> 14:56.080
The principal's leaving everything to us.

14:56.080 --> 14:58.540
And Akashi's at it again too, right?

14:58.540 --> 14:59.870
Yeah.

14:59.870 --> 15:01.330
With the Reaper.

15:02.330 --> 15:05.050
Why are they making Akashi take care of it alone?

15:10.220 --> 15:12.340
That's it for today.

15:12.340 --> 15:14.560
Just boarding it was progress.

15:14.560 --> 15:16.680
It certainly wasn't bad.

15:16.680 --> 15:19.730
He's still stable despite lowering the screen-out rate.

15:20.230 --> 15:21.770
What?

15:21.770 --> 15:24.610
Is he prepared to accept it?

15:33.030 --> 15:36.790
I'm sorry I couldn't watch over you today.

15:38.040 --> 15:41.580
For now, can you all gather in front of the hangar?

15:42.420 --> 15:44.000
Yes, then that's fine.

15:52.300 --> 15:53.680
Someone likes to make a mess.

16:03.350 --> 16:04.350
Whoops.

16:29.920 --> 16:30.590
What's wrong?

16:31.170 --> 16:32.470
The principal?

16:42.430 --> 16:43.980
An Admonition's appeared near the hangar!

16:44.850 --> 16:47.610
Team Gargouille is engaging it right now!

16:51.280 --> 16:54.360
Wait! Are you gonna send Akashi on the Argent?

16:54.360 --> 16:59.200
Don't you think it's a good chance to get field data?

16:59.200 --> 17:01.080
There are still too many things we don't know.

17:01.750 --> 17:04.830
If we just send it out there, there's no guarantee—

17:05.960 --> 17:07.540
The filters...

17:08.090 --> 17:09.290
What about the CEO's consent?

17:09.630 --> 17:12.920
It's more about the pilot's will.

17:12.920 --> 17:16.010
Do you think you can do it, Saginuma-kun?

17:18.970 --> 17:20.060
Akashi...

17:26.850 --> 17:28.060
We're going around!

17:28.060 --> 17:28.900
Roger!

17:32.940 --> 17:34.110
Don't get in our way!

17:34.110 --> 17:35.400
Stay back!

17:35.400 --> 17:36.030
Damn it!

17:42.160 --> 17:42.830
Why?

17:58.340 --> 18:00.350
What is that thing trying to do?

18:01.220 --> 18:03.140
Command module, retreat!

18:03.930 --> 18:04.730
Command module?

18:04.730 --> 18:06.060
We're getting out!

18:06.060 --> 18:07.350
Getting out?

18:07.350 --> 18:09.520
You're in our way, so leave at once!

18:18.860 --> 18:20.660
What now, Raika?

18:20.660 --> 18:23.290
We have to pull it away from the command module!

18:24.700 --> 18:25.500
Hey, Raika!

18:37.590 --> 18:38.180
Raika!

18:38.180 --> 18:39.470
Shit.

18:39.470 --> 18:42.140
I have no choice but to go.

18:44.770 --> 18:45.720
The Reaper?

18:47.680 --> 18:48.770
Akashi!

19:00.950 --> 19:03.080
Now's our chance! Hurry!

19:24.390 --> 19:25.760
Where's that girl?

19:26.220 --> 19:27.180
Over there!

19:29.230 --> 19:31.190
Akashi, by your feet!

19:32.770 --> 19:33.900
Sasame?

19:33.900 --> 19:35.400
What are you doing?!

19:35.400 --> 19:36.360
Hurry up and escape!

19:41.780 --> 19:43.030
She's crying?

19:52.750 --> 19:54.330
Sasame?

20:08.560 --> 20:09.770
Akashi!

20:46.640 --> 20:49.600
So that's your core, isn't it?!

21:02.150 --> 21:03.320
It ran!

21:13.750 --> 21:14.830
No...

21:16.370 --> 21:18.380
I want to play more...

21:19.710 --> 21:21.630
Play with me...

21:32.390 --> 21:34.810
That Admonition...

21:34.810 --> 21:36.020
Yeah.

21:36.020 --> 21:37.480
That just now...

21:38.310 --> 21:38.980
Yes.

21:42.900 --> 21:44.820
It was a child.

21:44.820 --> 21:45.490
Yeah.

21:47.030 --> 21:50.370
That child didn't get to play enough either.

21:50.990 --> 21:51.660
Yeah.

21:52.410 --> 21:55.410
That Admonition probably didn't...

22:00.590 --> 22:03.340
It was also trapped by its past.

22:04.550 --> 22:05.970
That Admonition...

22:12.260 --> 22:14.020
That went well.

22:14.020 --> 22:15.730
I expected nothing less.

22:15.730 --> 22:17.770
I'll report this to our superiors.

22:17.770 --> 22:19.600
Go right ahead.

22:19.600 --> 22:21.730
I'm sure they'll be in bliss.

22:21.730 --> 22:23.690
No doubt about it.

22:29.360 --> 22:31.240
I met Sasame...

22:32.700 --> 22:33.830
Sometime in the past...

22:44.840 --> 22:55.470
Throwing away all my excuses, I traced over my abrased heart

22:55.470 --> 23:00.020
In the coldness of the locker room,

23:00.020 --> 23:06.480
Was an unfulfilled promise, locked away

23:06.990 --> 23:12.950
Dispel the darkness in this fallen world,

23:12.950 --> 23:17.500
And give me a reason why I should continue living

23:17.500 --> 23:22.880
The meaning of good-byes, the expectations of people,

23:22.880 --> 23:27.760
And the melodies that we played while never crossing paths

23:27.760 --> 23:33.470
I know I must not run away. The only path is straight ahead

23:33.470 --> 23:37.970
Even if this turns out to be a mistake

23:37.970 --> 23:43.560
The whirlpools of destiny will consume all loneliness

23:43.560 --> 23:51.660
It is an unerasable scar, an egoism that cannot be discarded

24:05.090 --> 24:10.090
Episode 4

24:05.090 --> 24:10.090
Danger, Do Not Mix
